A||||5||87 Pegasus||Fiero Owner Needs Our Help... Please Read||||1||
Z||000000||87 Pegasus||11-30-2001||08:40 PM||||It sickens me to hear this... How could someone do this. He wanted me to e-mail everyone i knew in the Fiero world but i figured this was the easiest way to get the word out. So if you can help let me or Kevin know thank you ---------<BR>Gentlemen, Ladies -<BR>Could you please pass this on to anyone who shares an interest in <BR>Fieros for<BR>me?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Kevin A. Henry<P>Hello to all Fiero lovers!<BR>Bad news - my 85 GT was stolen last night (Nov 29, 2001) from my <BR>home<BR>in Arlington, TX. It's irreplaceable - only had 67000 miles on it. I <BR>had<BR>it parked and covered while I was slowly fixing the minor things and <BR>only<BR>drove it once in a while to keep it lubed up. I can't help but think <BR>that<BR>it was stolen just because it was a Fiero and someone needed parts.<BR>Hopefully I'm wrong and someone just wanted to take it for a joy ride - <BR>I<BR>don't like to think that a fellow Fiero owner-enthusiast would chop up <BR>a car<BR>like this one just for parts. If that's the case and the thief is <BR>reading<BR>this, I'll make a deal with you....if you bring back my 85 (or just <BR>leave it<BR>somewhere that it can be found in one piece) I'll gladly give you my 85 <BR>2m4<BR>and my 86 SE - both of which I was planning to rebuild in the future. <BR>If<BR>that's not enough, I'll give you my 84 SE as well - in perfect running<BR>shape; only needs minor cosmetics and I have the parts for the repairs. <BR>I<BR>just want my GT back.<BR>I can't understand why anyone would take this other than for <BR>parts. It<BR>was parked next to my 2000 Silverado, my roommate's 2001 S-10 Extreme, <BR>my<BR>brother's 94 conversion van, and our 95 Ford 15 passanger van. All of <BR>which<BR>are worth quite a bit more than my Fiero to the average thief. I hope <BR>this<BR>doesn't happen to anyone else who reads this. Be careful with your <BR>Fieros<BR>and don't let them disappear like mine did - they can never be <BR>replaced.<BR>Just in case anyone sees it or parts of it, it was an 85 GT, dark <BR>metallic<BR>blue (aftermarket paint) with 86GT alluminum/gray honeycomb mags (small<BR>chips on outside of wheel), sunroof, gray on gray interior with stich <BR>scars<BR>where the seats were repaired. If anyone can help me get it back <BR>somehow,<BR>I'll gladly offer them the same deal on my other Fieros...no questions<BR>asked, of course...no police involvement, totally anonymous.<BR>I can be reached at khenry@peoplepc.com or on my cell phone<BR>(817)800-4399. Any help would be greatly appreciated -<BR>Thanks,<BR>Kevin A. Henry<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367_3.gif"> <BR>God Bless America....<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||1
